   "source": [
    "# Ireland Electricity Price Analytics\n",
    "\n",
    "**Project 02 — Ireland / Energy / Data**\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook analyses how Irish business electricity prices changed from 2015–2025, places that decade inside a longer 2008–2025 history, compares electricity with business gas prices, examines differences across business consumption bands, and prepares the dataset for later demand × price and forecasting work.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Core research question\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Why did Irish business electricity prices change so sharply, who paid what, and which variables should we carry into a defensible 2026–2035 forecasting model?**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Publication phase:** historical analysis, market-driver testing, model validation and 2026–2035 scenario modelling are complete.  \n",
    "**Forecasting approach:** the project reports transparent scenarios rather than presenting one long-run point estimate as certain.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f21250a6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Source hierarchy\n",
    "\n",
    "Primary sources used in this version:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **SEAI Energy Price Trends** — weighted-average business electricity and gas prices.\n",
    "2. **SEAI EPR Semester Update, July–December 2025** — 2025 S2 weighted average, business consumption-band prices, EU ranking and market shares.\n",
    "3. **SEAI Commercial Fuel Cost Comparison** — supporting quarterly fuel-cost context.\n",
    "\n",
    "Official links:\n",
    "- https://www.seai.ie/data-and-insights/seai-statistics/prices\n",
    "- https://www.seai.ie/data-and-insights/seai-statistics/energy-prices\n",
    "- https://www.seai.ie/sites/default/files/publications/EPR-Electricity-Gas-Prices.pdf\n",
    "\n",
    "**Important:** the commercial fuel-cost table is not treated as 72 independent electricity-price observations because electricity/gas values repeat across many adjacent quarters. The biannual EPR series is our main target-price series.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Publication summary\n",
    "\n",
    "Key findings from the completed analysis:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Weighted-average Irish business electricity prices rose from **13.79 c/kWh in 2015** to **23.49 c/kWh in 2025** on an annual-average basis.\n",
    "- The semester peak was **28.40 c/kWh in 2022 S2**, during the European energy-price shock.\n",
    "- In 2025 S2, the largest public non-household consumption band (**IG, >150,000 MWh/year**) paid **15.9 c/kWh**, compared with a **22.7 c/kWh** weighted business average.\n",
    "- On 2018–2025 walk-forward validation, a simple **last-price naive model** beat Holt, trend and gas-augmented alternatives.\n",
    "- Adding lagged wholesale features improved explanation but **did not beat the naive baseline out of sample**.\n",
    "- The long-run output is therefore a **scenario envelope**, not a single deterministic price forecast. For weighted-average business prices in real 2025 money, the 2035 scenarios are approximately **21.2 / 24.4 / 30.1 c/kWh** (low / central / high).\n",
    "\n",
    "These scenarios are analytical sensitivities, not official forecasts or statistical confidence intervals.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ee75d366",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
