  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "213b1934",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Validate the source snapshots\n",
    "\n",
    "Before analysing prices, check period uniqueness, numeric coverage, expected time ranges and missing values.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "692c4725",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def validate_period_table(df, period_col):\n",
    "    print(\"Rows:\", len(df))\n",
    "    print(\"Unique periods:\", df[period_col].nunique())\n",
    "    print(\"Duplicate periods:\", int(df[period_col].duplicated().sum()))\n",
    "    print(\"First period:\", df[period_col].iloc[0])\n",
    "    print(\"Last period:\", df[period_col].iloc[-1])\n",
    "    print(\"\\nMissing values:\")\n",
    "    display(df.isna().sum().to_frame(\"missing\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"BUSINESS ELECTRICITY\")\n",
    "validate_period_table(electricity, \"period\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nBUSINESS GAS\")\n",
    "validate_period_table(gas, \"period\")\n",
    "\n",
    "assert electricity[\"period\"].is_unique\n",
    "assert gas[\"period\"].is_unique\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "76fbcab4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Data-quality note: “quarterly” does not mean quarterly-independent\n",
    "\n",
    "The SEAI commercial fuel comparison is published as a quarterly series, but business electricity and gas values often repeat across adjacent quarters. That makes it useful as contextual fuel-cost history, but not a good excuse to artificially inflate the target-price sample size.\n",
    "\n",
    "The direct EPR business-price series is collected and reported **biannually**, so the forecasting target will preserve that cadence unless we later obtain a genuinely higher-frequency market-price target.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e2e8d380",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "repeat_rate_electricity = (\n",
    "    quarterly_fuels[\"electricity_avg_commercial_c_per_kwh\"]\n",
    "    .diff()\n",
    "    .eq(0)\n",
    "    .mean()\n",
    ")\n",
    "repeat_rate_gas = (\n",
    "    quarterly_fuels[\"gas_avg_commercial_c_per_kwh\"]\n",
    "    .diff()\n",
    "    .eq(0)\n",
    "    .mean()\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Adjacent-quarter repeats — electricity: {repeat_rate_electricity:.1%}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Adjacent-quarter repeats — gas: {repeat_rate_gas:.1%}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "685f41ed",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Build the core biannual business-price dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "We combine Irish weighted-average business electricity and gas prices at the same semester frequency.\n",
    "\n",
    "Prices are in **euro cent/kWh, ex VAT**.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d5aec167",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "prices = (\n",
    "    electricity[[\"period\", \"ireland_c_per_kwh\", \"euro_area_c_per_kwh\", \"eu27_c_per_kwh\"]]\n",
    "    .rename(columns={\n",
    "        \"ireland_c_per_kwh\": \"electricity_ie_c_per_kwh\",\n",
    "        \"euro_area_c_per_kwh\": \"electricity_euro_area_c_per_kwh\",\n",
    "        \"eu27_c_per_kwh\": \"electricity_eu27_c_per_kwh\",\n",
    "    })\n",
    "    .merge(\n",
    "        gas[[\"period\", \"ireland_c_per_kwh\"]]\n",
    "        .rename(columns={\"ireland_c_per_kwh\": \"gas_ie_c_per_kwh\"}),\n",
    "        on=\"period\",\n",
    "        how=\"left\",\n",
    "        validate=\"one_to_one\",\n",
    "    )\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "prices[\"year\"] = prices[\"period\"].str[:4].astype(int)\n",
    "prices[\"semester\"] = prices[\"period\"].str[-1].astype(int)\n",
    "prices[\"electricity_yoy_pct\"] = prices[\"electricity_ie_c_per_kwh\"].pct_change(2) * 100\n",
    "prices[\"gas_yoy_pct\"] = prices[\"gas_ie_c_per_kwh\"].pct_change(2) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "prices.to_csv(PROCESSED_DIR / \"business_energy_prices_biannual_2008_2025.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "display(prices.tail(10))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c8e1c0c5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. The 2015–2025 story window\n",
    "\n",
    "The public-facing story will align with Project 01's decade. The modelling history remains longer.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "06c17128",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "story = prices.query(\"2015 <= year <= 2025\").copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "annual = (\n",
    "    story.groupby(\"year\", as_index=False)\n",
    "    .agg(\n",
    "        business_electricity_c_per_kwh=(\"electricity_ie_c_per_kwh\", \"mean\"),\n",
    "        business_gas_c_per_kwh=(\"gas_ie_c_per_kwh\", \"mean\"),\n",
    "    )\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "annual[\"electricity_yoy_pct\"] = annual[\"business_electricity_c_per_kwh\"].pct_change() * 100\n",
    "annual[\"gas_yoy_pct\"] = annual[\"business_gas_c_per_kwh\"].pct_change() * 100\n",
    "annual.to_csv(PROCESSED_DIR / \"business_energy_prices_annual_2015_2025.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "p2015 = annual.loc[annual[\"year\"].eq(2015), \"business_electricity_c_per_kwh\"].iloc[0]\n",
    "p2025 = annual.loc[annual[\"year\"].eq(2025), \"business_electricity_c_per_kwh\"].iloc[0]\n",
    "peak = prices.loc[prices[\"electricity_ie_c_per_kwh\"].idxmax()]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"2015 annual average: {p2015:.2f} c/kWh\")\n",
    "print(f\"2025 annual average: {p2025:.2f} c/kWh\")\n",
    "print(f\"2015→2025 change: {(p2025/p2015-1)*100:.1f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"Peak semester: {peak['period']} at {peak['electricity_ie_c_per_kwh']:.1f} c/kWh\")\n",
    "print(f\"2025 S2: {prices.iloc[-1]['electricity_ie_c_per_kwh']:.1f} c/kWh\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
