    "### First finding\n",
    "\n",
    "The decade is **not** a smooth upward trend.\n",
    "\n",
    "Business electricity prices were relatively stable through 2020, rose sharply during the 2021–2022 European energy shock, peaked at **28.4 c/kWh in 2022 S2**, then partially retreated. The 2025 S2 weighted average was **22.7 c/kWh** — about 20% below the peak, but still materially above the pre-crisis level.\n"
   ]
  },
