   "source": [
    "## 7. What we can say already\n",
    "\n",
    "From the first official datasets:\n",
    "\n",
    "- The 2015–2025 business electricity annual average increased by roughly **70%**.\n",
    "- The decade contains a major structural break around the 2021–2022 energy crisis; a simple straight-line forecast would be inappropriate.\n",
    "- Electricity and business gas prices are strongly correlated over the full sample, but the relationship becomes much stronger during/after 2021.\n",
    "- Ireland's business electricity price remains high in European comparison.\n",
    "- Very large users pay substantially less per kWh than small users, so the later Demand × Price project must not apply an average business tariff directly to data-centre consumption.\n",
    "\n",
    "These findings determine the next data-engineering step.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0b51580a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Next research layer before forecasting\n",
    "\n",
    "We will now add variables that can plausibly explain price movement:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **SEMOpx wholesale electricity price** — preferably monthly or daily aggregated to semester/quarter.\n",
    "2. **CRU network tariff / allowed revenue series** — network-cost component.\n",
    "3. **SEAI / CSO electricity demand and generation mix** — demand, wind, gas generation and imports.\n",
    "4. **Project 01 data-centre demand** — joined only after the price model is independently understood.\n",
    "5. **Eurostat price components** — energy/supply, networks, taxes/levies where comparable.\n",
    "\n",
    "Only then will we compare:\n",
    "- naive baseline\n",
    "- Holt / ETS\n",
    "- ARIMA/SARIMA\n",
    "- regression with exogenous variables\n",
    "- regularised regression / tree model only if sample size supports it\n",
    "\n",
    "Validation will use **walk-forward / rolling-origin evaluation**, never a random split.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Wholesale electricity layer\n",
    "\n",
    "Retail electricity prices do not move independently of the wholesale market.\n",
    "\n",
    "For this project we use two complementary official measures:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **CSO WPM37** — monthly Wholesale Price Index for Electricity. This becomes our higher-frequency modelling feature.\n",
    "- **SEMOpx Day-Ahead Market (DAM)** — annual average clearing-price benchmarks in €/MWh. This gives the wholesale series an interpretable absolute-price scale.\n",
    "\n",
    "CSO states that from January 2019 onward its electricity index uses the Day-Ahead Single Market Price. The 2021=100 rebasing changes the scale, not the underlying month-to-month price movement.\n",
    "\n",
    "Sources:\n",
    "- CSO WPM37 dataset: https://ws.cso.ie/public/api.restful/PxStat.Data.Cube_API.ReadDataset/WPM37/CSV/1.0/en\n",
    "- CSO methodology: https://www.cso.ie/en/methods/prices/wholesalepriceindex/introductionofupdatedppiwpiseriesbaseyear2021100/chapter3examplesofchangestoseries/\n",
    "- SEMOpx historical-data guide: https://www.semopx.com/market-data/static-reports/semopx-historical-market-data-final-v2.pdf\n"
