  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Download the official monthly CSO wholesale-electricity index\n",
    "\n",
    "This cell downloads the complete **WPM37** table directly from the CSO PXStat API and saves the raw snapshot in the project.\n",
    "\n",
    "The parser is deliberately tolerant of PXStat column-name changes: it detects the month, energy type and value fields rather than assuming a fixed column order.\n"
   ],
   "id": "Qz_Y6rkum-q2"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import requests\n",
    "import re\n",
    "\n",
    "CSO_WPM37_URL = (\n",
    "    \"https://ws.cso.ie/public/api.restful/\"\n",
    "    \"PxStat.Data.Cube_API.ReadDataset/WPM37/CSV/1.0/en\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "WPM37_RAW = RAW_DIR / \"cso_wpm37_wholesale_energy.csv\"\n",
    "\n",
    "if not WPM37_RAW.exists():\n",
    "    response = requests.get(CSO_WPM37_URL, timeout=60)\n",
    "    response.raise_for_status()\n",
    "    WPM37_RAW.write_bytes(response.content)\n",
    "    print(\"Downloaded:\", WPM37_RAW)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Using existing raw snapshot:\", WPM37_RAW)\n",
    "\n",
    "wpm37 = pd.read_csv(WPM37_RAW)\n",
    "print(\"Rows:\", len(wpm37))\n",
    "print(\"Columns:\", list(wpm37.columns))\n",
    "display(wpm37.head())\n"
   ],
   "id": "fGzukfDum-q2"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def find_col(columns, include_any, exclude_any=()):\n",
    "    for col in columns:\n",
    "        low = str(col).lower()\n",
    "        if any(token in low for token in include_any) and not any(token in low for token in exclude_any):\n",
    "            return col\n",
    "    return None\n",
    "\n",
    "month_col = find_col(wpm37.columns, [\"month\"])\n",
    "energy_col = find_col(wpm37.columns, [\"type of energy\", \"energy\"])\n",
    "value_col = next((c for c in wpm37.columns if str(c).strip().upper() == \"VALUE\"), None)\n",
    "\n",
    "if month_col is None:\n",
    "    # PXStat files often include a TLIST(M1) monthly code.\n",
    "    month_col = find_col(wpm37.columns, [\"tlist\"])\n",
    "if energy_col is None or value_col is None or month_col is None:\n",
    "    raise ValueError(\n",
    "        f\"Could not identify required WPM37 columns. \"\n",
    "        f\"month={month_col}, energy={energy_col}, value={value_col}\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "wholesale = wpm37[\n",
    "    wpm37[energy_col].astype(str).str.contains(\"electricity\", case=False, na=False)\n",
    "].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Prefer the human-readable month label; if it is a numeric code, handle YYYYMM.\n",
    "month_text = wholesale[month_col].astype(str).str.strip()\n",
    "parsed_date = pd.to_datetime(month_text, errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if parsed_date.isna().mean() > 0.5:\n",
    "    digits = month_text.str.replace(r\"\\D\", \"\", regex=True)\n",
    "    parsed_date = pd.to_datetime(digits.str[:6], format=\"%Y%m\", errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "\n",
    "wholesale[\"date\"] = parsed_date\n",
    "wholesale[\"wholesale_electricity_index\"] = pd.to_numeric(\n",
    "    wholesale[value_col], errors=\"coerce\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "wholesale = (\n",
    "    wholesale[[\"date\", \"wholesale_electricity_index\"]]\n",
    "    .dropna()\n",
    "    .drop_duplicates(subset=[\"date\"])\n",
    "    .sort_values(\"date\")\n",
    "    .reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "display(wholesale.head())\n",
    "display(wholesale.tail())\n",
    "\n",
    "wholesale.to_csv(\n",
    "    PROCESSED_DIR / \"cso_wholesale_electricity_monthly.csv\",\n",
    "    index=False,\n",
    ")\n"
   ],
   "id": "2NI2FflGm-q2"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "story_wholesale = wholesale[\n",
    "    wholesale[\"date\"].between(\"2015-01-01\", \"2025-12-31\")\n",
    "].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 5.8))\n",
    "ax.plot(\n",
    "    story_wholesale[\"date\"],\n",
    "    story_wholesale[\"wholesale_electricity_index\"],\n",
    "    linewidth=2.0,\n",
    ")\n",
    "ax.axhline(100, linewidth=1, linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.6)\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Ireland wholesale electricity price index, 2015–2025\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Index (2021 average = 100)\")\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"\")\n",
    "ax.grid(axis=\"y\", alpha=0.25)\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ],
   "id": "cYXXACB4m-q2"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 11. Does wholesale movement lead retail prices?\n",
    "\n",
    "Retail prices are observed every six months, so we aggregate the monthly wholesale index to the same semester frequency.\n",
    "\n",
    "Then we test:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Lag 0:** wholesale and retail in the same semester\n",
    "- **Lag 1:** wholesale leads retail by one semester\n",
    "- **Lag 2:** wholesale leads retail by one year\n",
    "- up to **Lag 4**\n",
    "\n",
    "These are relationship diagnostics, not causal estimates.\n"
   ],
   "id": "sMDTZLPsm-q3"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "wholesale_half = wholesale.copy()\n",
    "wholesale_half[\"year\"] = wholesale_half[\"date\"].dt.year\n",
    "wholesale_half[\"semester\"] = np.where(\n",
    "    wholesale_half[\"date\"].dt.month <= 6, \"S1\", \"S2\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "wholesale_half[\"period\"] = (\n",
    "    wholesale_half[\"year\"].astype(str) + wholesale_half[\"semester\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "wholesale_half = (\n",
    "    wholesale_half.groupby([\"year\", \"semester\", \"period\"], as_index=False)\n",
    "    [\"wholesale_electricity_index\"]\n",
    "    .mean()\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "retail_half = prices[\n",
    "    [\"period\", \"year\", \"semester\", \"electricity_ie_c_per_kwh\"]\n",
    "].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "wholesale_retail = (\n",
    "    retail_half.merge(\n",
    "        wholesale_half[[\"period\", \"wholesale_electricity_index\"]],\n",
    "        on=\"period\",\n",
    "        how=\"inner\",\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    .sort_values([\"year\", \"semester\"])\n",
    "    .reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Normalise both to their 2021 annual average = 100 for shape comparison.\n",
    "base_2021 = wholesale_retail.query(\"year == 2021\")\n",
    "retail_base = base_2021[\"electricity_ie_c_per_kwh\"].mean()\n",
    "wholesale_base = base_2021[\"wholesale_electricity_index\"].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "wholesale_retail[\"retail_index_2021_100\"] = (\n",
    "    wholesale_retail[\"electricity_ie_c_per_kwh\"] / retail_base * 100\n",
    ")\n",
    "wholesale_retail[\"wholesale_index_2021_100\"] = (\n",
    "    wholesale_retail[\"wholesale_electricity_index\"] / wholesale_base * 100\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "display(wholesale_retail.tail(12))\n",
    "\n",
    "wholesale_retail.to_csv(\n",
    "    PROCESSED_DIR / \"wholesale_retail_halfyear.csv\",\n",
    "    index=False,\n",
    ")\n"
   ],
   "id": "05I4AALfm-q3"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 5.8))\n",
    "ax.plot(\n",
    "    wholesale_retail[\"period\"],\n",
    "    wholesale_retail[\"retail_index_2021_100\"],\n",
    "    marker=\"o\",\n",
    "    label=\"Business retail price\",\n",
    ")\n",
    "ax.plot(\n",
    "    wholesale_retail[\"period\"],\n",
    "    wholesale_retail[\"wholesale_index_2021_100\"],\n",
    "    marker=\"o\",\n",
    "    label=\"Wholesale electricity\",\n",
    ")\n",
    "ax.axhline(100, linewidth=1, linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.6)\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Retail and wholesale electricity prices — normalised comparison\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Index (2021 average = 100)\")\n",
    "ax.tick_params(axis=\"x\", rotation=60)\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "ax.grid(axis=\"y\", alpha=0.25)\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ],
   "id": "uZ2mTsaGm-q3"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "lag_results = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for lag in range(5):\n",
    "    temp = wholesale_retail[\n",
    "        [\"electricity_ie_c_per_kwh\", \"wholesale_electricity_index\"]\n",
    "    ].copy()\n",
    "    temp[\"wholesale_lead\"] = temp[\"wholesale_electricity_index\"].shift(lag)\n",
    "    valid = temp.dropna()\n",
    "    lag_results.append({\n",
    "        \"wholesale_lead_semesters\": lag,\n",
    "        \"observations\": len(valid),\n",
    "        \"correlation\": valid[\"electricity_ie_c_per_kwh\"].corr(\n",
    "            valid[\"wholesale_lead\"]\n",
    "        ),\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "lag_results = pd.DataFrame(lag_results)\n",
    "display(lag_results)\n",
    "\n",
    "lag_results.to_csv(\n",
    "    PROCESSED_DIR / \"wholesale_retail_lag_correlations.csv\",\n",
    "    index=False,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9, 5))\n",
    "ax.bar(\n",
    "    lag_results[\"wholesale_lead_semesters\"].astype(str),\n",
    "    lag_results[\"correlation\"],\n",
    ")\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Wholesale-leading-retail correlation by lag\")\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Wholesale lead (semesters)\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Pearson correlation\")\n",
    "ax.axhline(0, linewidth=1)\n",
    "ax.grid(axis=\"y\", alpha=0.25)\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ],
   "id": "BywokTTym-q3"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### How to read the lag test\n",
    "\n",
    "The strongest lag is a **candidate feature relationship**, not proof that wholesale prices cause the observed retail movement by exactly that delay.\n",
    "\n",
    "Supplier hedging, contract structures, network tariffs, taxes/levies and other market effects can all alter the timing and magnitude of retail-price changes.\n",
    "\n",
    "The next model-building stage will compare predictive performance with and without lagged wholesale features using walk-forward validation.\n"
   ],
