   "source": [
    "## 13. Price components and network context\n",
    "\n",
    "A retail electricity price is not just the wholesale energy price.\n",
    "\n",
    "SEAI describes the non-household weighted-average bill as a combination of:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Energy and Supply**\n",
    "- **Network Costs**\n",
    "- **VAT**\n",
    "- **Renewable Taxes**\n",
    "- **Capacity Taxes**\n",
    "- **Environmental Taxes**\n",
    "- **Other**\n",
    "\n",
    "Eurostat publishes the same component framework for non-household consumption bands in dataset `nrg_pc_205_c`, with annual coverage from 2017 onward.\n",
    "\n",
    "For our modelling, components are primarily **explanatory and scenario variables**. We should not insert an annual network-cost series into a half-yearly forecast unless its timing and unit are aligned correctly.\n"
   ],
   "id": "_8Bso4YxyKDJ"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},